## Gate 2 — Every route and `?tab=` view has a test

**Rule.** Every wouter route and every `?tab=` view has at least one test that renders that surface and asserts on its content. Adding a route or a tab without that test fails the gate.

**Verify.**

```bash
rg -n "<Route" client/src/App.tsx
rg -n "export type ViewType" client/src/components/ViewTabs.tsx
rg -n --glob '*.test.tsx' "tab=|/terms|/404|TermsOfService|NotFound" client/src
pnpm test
```

List routes from `client/src/App.tsx`: every `<Route path="...">` plus the pathless `<Route>` catch-all. Today: `/` (Home), `/terms` (TermsOfService), `/404` (NotFound), catch-all (NotFound). The router base is `import.meta.env.BASE_URL` (Vite `base` in `vite.config.ts`: `/OWASP-AGENTIC-to-NIST-800-53v5-to-AI-RMF/`).

List tabs from the `ViewType` union in `client/src/components/ViewTabs.tsx`. `useTabParam` (`client/src/hooks/useTabParam.ts`) reads `?tab=` and defaults to `overview`. Today: `overview`, `matrix`, `aiRmf`, `detail`, `simulator`. When `analyze` joins that union, it is in scope immediately.

Vitest includes `client/src/**/*.test.{ts,tsx}` (`vitest.config.ts`). A surface is covered only when a test mounts the app at that path or `?tab=` value and asserts on content that belongs to that surface. Rendering a child component by itself does not cover the tab. `?risk=` is not a separate view.

**Pass.** `pnpm test` exits 0, and every path and every `ViewType` member has a matching render-and-assert test.

**Fail.** Add the missing test. Re-run `pnpm test` and the `rg` commands. Loop until every route and tab is covered. Do not delete a route or a tab to shrink the list.

## Gate 3 — WCAG 2.2 AA before merge

**Rule.** Automated accessibility checks run against every route and every `?tab=` view. Serious and critical violations are zero. CI must run the same check on pull requests before merge. Agents do not edit `.github/` to install that step; put the proposed job in the PR description for Shanti.

**Verify.** jsdom cannot measure contrast or reflow. The checker is `@axe-core/playwright` (axe-core), run by Playwright, one page per route and per `?tab=`. The script is `pnpm test:a11y`. It is not in `package.json` today. A missing script is a failure. An empty script, a skipped tag, or a shortened page list is a weakened check.

```bash
set -euo pipefail
# Fail if pinch-zoom is locked. WCAG 2.2 AA 1.4.4 / 1.4.10.
# rg exits 1 when the meta is clean; the if-form treats that as a pass.
if rg -n "maximum-scale|user-scalable" client/index.html; then exit 1; fi
pnpm test:a11y
```

`pnpm test:a11y` must, on `/`, `/terms`, `/404`, one unknown catch-all path, and `/?tab=` for each `ViewType` value:

- Run axe and fail on any violation whose impact is `serious` or `critical`.
- Assert landmarks `header`, `nav`, `main`, and `footer`.
- Assert a skip link whose target is `main`.
- Assert every form control and every icon-only button has an accessible name.
- Assert color contrast at WCAG 2.2 AA.
- Assert the page is usable at 200% zoom and at 400% (reflow at 320 CSS pixels wide: no clipped primary content, no horizontal scroll for text).

**Pass.** The viewport grep finds nothing. `pnpm test:a11y` exits 0 with zero serious or critical violations on every route and tab. The PR description contains the `ci.yml` step Shanti must add so the command runs on `pull_request` before merge. Do not merge on the strength of a local run alone once that step exists; until Shanti adds it, say in the PR that CI does not run it yet.

**Fail.** Fix the UI. Re-run the grep and `pnpm test:a11y`. Loop until both pass. Do not disable an axe rule, drop a page, or remove `maximum-scale` from the check to get green.

## Gate 4 — Dependencies and secrets

**Rule.** Dependency vulnerabilities at high or critical fail the gate. A leaked secret fails the gate. No secret is read from a `VITE_` variable. Vite inlines `import.meta.env.VITE_*` into the client bundle.

**Verify.**

```bash
set -euo pipefail
pnpm audit --audit-level high
gitleaks detect --source . --redact --no-banner
# rg exits 1 when there is no match. A match is a failure.
if rg -n "VITE_[A-Z0-9_]*(KEY|SECRET|TOKEN|PASSWORD|CREDENTIAL)" \
  client packages --glob '!**/node_modules/**' --glob '!**/dist/**'; then
  exit 1
fi
if git ls-files | rg -n '(^|/)\.env($|\.)'; then exit 1; fi
```

`gitleaks` is the secret scanner to use. It is not installed by `pnpm install`. If the binary is missing, install it and re-run. Do not skip the scan, and do not substitute a hand-rolled grep for it. Trufflehog is acceptable only when gitleaks cannot be installed; say so in the PR. Low and moderate audit findings do not fail this gate. Do not lower `--audit-level` below `high`, and do not add an audit ignore, to get green.

**Pass.** `pnpm audit --audit-level high` exits 0. `gitleaks detect` exits 0. The `VITE_` grep finds nothing. No `.env` file is tracked.

**Fail.** Upgrade or remove the vulnerable dependency, or rotate and purge the leaked secret, then re-run. Loop until all four commands pass. If a high or critical advisory has no fix, stop and say so in the PR. Shanti decides. Do not silence it.

## Gate 5 — No stack traces in the UI

**Rule.** An error boundary wraps the app and renders a short friendly message. The UI never shows a stack trace.

**Verify.**

```bash
rg -n "\.stack" client/src --glob '!*.test.ts' --glob '!*.test.tsx'
```

**Pass.** The command prints nothing (`rg` exits 1 when it finds nothing; that is a pass). `client/src/App.tsx` still mounts an error boundary, and the boundary's rendered output is a friendly message plus a way to reload. `console.error` of the error object in development is allowed. Reading or rendering `.stack` is not.

**Fail.** Remove the stack from the rendered tree. Re-run the grep. Loop until it prints nothing. Do not delete the error boundary to make the grep pass.

## Gate 6 — Bundle budget

**Rule.** The production bundle stays within the gzip ceilings below. Ceilings are 10% above the `main` build measured 2026-11-20 (`gzip -c -9`). Load-time and LCP are not this gate; they are `[manual]` in `agent-constraints.mdc` (no Lighthouse script in this repo).

**Verify.** After `pnpm build`:

```bash
set -euo pipefail
fail=0
check() {
  local label="$1" limit="$2" bytes="$3"
  if [ "$bytes" -gt "$limit" ]; then echo "FAIL $label gzip=$bytes limit=$limit"; fail=1
  else echo "ok $label gzip=$bytes limit=$limit"; fi
}
shopt -s nullglob
mains=(dist/public/assets/index-*.js)
csss=(dist/public/assets/index-*.css)
[ "${#mains[@]}" -eq 1 ] && [ "${#csss[@]}" -eq 1 ]
check "main-js" 242000 "$(gzip -c -9 "${mains[0]}" | wc -c | tr -d ' ')"
check "css" 15000 "$(gzip -c -9 "${csss[0]}" | wc -c | tr -d ' ')"
total=0
for f in dist/public/assets/*.js; do
  bytes="$(gzip -c -9 "$f" | wc -c | tr -d ' ')"
  total=$((total + bytes))
  case "$(basename "$f")" in
    index-*) ;;
    *) check "chunk $(basename "$f")" 47000 "$bytes" ;;
  esac
done
check "js-total" 289000 "$total"
exit "$fail"
```

Ceilings, in gzip bytes: main entry `index-*.js` ≤ 242000; each other JS chunk ≤ 47000; `index-*.css` ≤ 15000; all JS summed ≤ 289000. Exactly one `index-*.js` and one `index-*.css`. Measured that day: main 220004, CSS 13352, `ScenarioSimulator` chunk 42603, JS total 262607.

**Pass.** The script exits 0.

**Fail.** Shrink the bundle. Re-run Gate 1 and this script. Loop until both pass. Do not raise a ceiling, and do not split chunks only to duck the `index-*` count, to get green. Clearing this gate does not clear Gate 1's raw chunk-size warning.
